{"findings":[{"id":"4209e603-e565-40bb-b9d9-7754cb40e5a2","title":"A later tap's no-match message is hidden","description":"`pushed` resets `said`, but a delayed `retry` for an earlier push sets it again because the handler checks only the device ID, not the push times in `d.pushes`. If the later push was silently dropped, its own timer emits `nomatch`, but `!said` is false and the earlier push's sticky “Try again” message remains.","category":"Correctness","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"implemented","git_sha":"1306dc9550075866fb556726e87e1526b70fe4b9","location":{"file_path":"web/index.html","start_line":377,"end_line":380,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/index.html[370-380]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[133-137]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[158-164]"}]}},{"id":"07c384af-9671-437a-83c4-3b427ff9f947","title":"A leader change hides a valid join result","description":"`fromLeader()` checks a result against the receiver’s current `s.leader`, rather than the leader that decided the push. If the old time keeper resolves a join between devices that remain in the room and then leaves before its `joined` broadcast arrives, those devices elect a successor and discard the in-flight result.","category":"Correctness","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"1306dc9550075866fb556726e87e1526b70fe4b9","location":{"file_path":"web/net.js","start_line":150,"end_line":151,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[33-52]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[110-116]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[127-153]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/index.html[364-369]"}]}},{"id":"4bf90ebe-18fb-43ef-8cbe-b845d9227735","title":"Join tests skip non-facing and edge taps","description":"The new join checks in `tests/two-browser.mjs` and `tests/net.test.mjs` start every join through direct `net.push` calls, so no test sends a tap from a strip or a tap position. Non-facing taps, endpoint positions and default keyboard positions are never exercised. Strip-based stacking and overlap are deferred by the author's stated scope, so this is a known gap rather than a defect in the shipped path, but a later change could join ineligible taps without any failing check.","category":"Maintainability","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"1306dc9550075866fb556726e87e1526b70fe4b9","location":{"file_path":"tests/two-browser.mjs","start_line":67,"end_line":69,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"ticket","source":"https://github.com/jtbinith/qodo-hack-2026/issues/68"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/two-browser.mjs[67-69]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/net.test.mjs[59-72]"}]}}],"finding_state":{"complete":true,"introduced":[],"resolved":["4209e603-e565-40bb-b9d9-7754cb40e5a2"],"still_open":["07c384af-9671-437a-83c4-3b427ff9f947","4bf90ebe-18fb-43ef-8cbe-b845d9227735"],"dismissed":[]},"review_agent_comment":"Nothing to comment.","meta":{"analysis":{"baseline_checkpoint_id":"47c65b6b3cf748d09457e001b241508d","mode":"incremental","reason":"changes_since_checkpoint"},"checkpoint":{"base_sha":"1306dc9550075866fb556726e87e1526b70fe4b9","coverage_started_at":"2026-11-21T12:19:04.020185+00:00","created_at":"2026-11-21T12:37:38.944447+00:00","id":"df03d0c6838e408995e8d544fb8967dd","sequence":37058,"tree_sha":"a867c56fb94bc329daf99685d6d6fe8ce1b84c8e","version":1},"context":{"author_notes":{"input_chars":2192,"max_tokens":16000,"offloaded":false,"original_tokens":531,"outcome":"inline","rendered_chars":2362},"ticket_bodies":[{"index":1,"input_chars":17421,"max_tokens":5000,"offloaded":false,"original_tokens":4355,"outcome":"inline","rendered_chars":17421},{"index":2,"input_chars":1172,"max_tokens":5000,"offloa